full_details:
abt global llc
agency: department of the interior
public involvement planning, outreach, and facilitation services for renewable energy activities in the gulf of mexico (gomr) - task order: public involvement planning, outreach, and facilitation services for renewable energy activities in the gulf of america (goar)

grant to university of california, merced
agency: national endowment for the humanities
renovations in the kolligian library at the university of california, merced, to create a regional archive focused on the central valley and sierra nevada in california.&nbsp;

grant to university of north carolina
agency: national endowment for the humanities
production of a ninety-minute film about the 1898 violent overthrow of elected officials in wilmington, north carolina, and its economic and political legacy.&nbsp;

grant to city lore, inc.
agency: national endowment for the humanities
production of a documentary film on the life and work of the chicano playwright, producer, and activist luis valdez.&nbsp;&nbsp;

grant to united society of shakers, sabbathday lake, inc.
agency: national endowment for the humanities
renovation of an 1824 herb house as a work, education, and display space linked to the folkways and history of the sabbathday lake shakers near new gloucester, maine.&nbsp;

grant to saint anselm college
agency: national endowment for the humanities
renovation of a 1913 campus building at saint anselm college, new hampshire, to establish dedicated space for the grappone humanities institute.&nbsp;&nbsp;

grant to carnegie library of homestead
agency: national endowment for the humanities
renovation of the carnegie library of homestead’s 1898 building to include new hvac, fire suppression, plumbing, electrical, and ada upgrades that will expand accessibility, support an increase in humanities programming, and enhance safety for patrons and library staff.&nbsp;

grant to historic albany foundation, inc.
agency: national endowment for the humanities
restoration of the oldest building in albany, new york, the van ostrande-radliff house from 1728, and its later additions, to serve as the seat of the historic albany foundation.&nbsp;

grant to juniata college
agency: national endowment for the humanities
renovation of the archives at juniata college in huntingdon, pa, to consolidate and preserve the library’s collections, including significant american anabaptist history materials.&nbsp;

grant to fort ross conservancy
agency: national endowment for the humanities
production of a film examining the displacement and homeland restoration of the kashia-pomo, a small tribal nation from the sonoma county, california, region.&nbsp;

grant to american film institute
agency: national endowment for the humanities
the expansion of the&nbsp;<em>afi catalog</em>,&nbsp;the filmographic online database&nbsp;which documents&nbsp;the first 100 years of american cinema,&nbsp;by adding&nbsp;45,000&nbsp;titles and associated data for short films released from 1893&nbsp;to 1933 and completing 6,000&nbsp;records of short films&nbsp;from&nbsp;the silent film era.&nbsp;&nbsp;

grant to university of missouri system
agency: national endowment for the humanities
two week-long workshops focused on the “golden age” of the 1920s and 1930s in kansas city for a total of 72 k-12 teachers and museum educators. &nbsp;

grant to center for independent documentary, inc.
agency: national endowment for the humanities
development of a feature length documentary about the figure of the cowboy in american popular imagination and its role in shaping myths and identities throughout u.s. history.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;

grant to western carolina university
agency: national endowment for the humanities
preparation for an annotated translation of a series of critical editions, with digital components, of handwritten eastern cherokee social documents from the mid 1880s to the early 1990s. (12 months)&nbsp;

grant to dr. laura beth mcgrath
agency: national endowment for the humanities
research and writing for a book examining the role of the literary agent in shaping the marketplace and the literary attitudes of readers.&nbsp;

grant to dr. andrew newman
agency: national endowment for the humanities
research and writing for a book examining american high school english curriculum as a touchstone of american literary history and culture.&nbsp;

grant to dr. joan victoria flores-villalobos
agency: national endowment for the humanities
research and writing leading to a book about the ecological and social dimensions of gold extraction in amazonian venezuela between 1849 and the early 1900s. &nbsp;

grant to dr. chunmei du
agency: national endowment for the humanities
research and writing leading to a book on the us occupation of china at the end of world war ii, focused on everyday encounters between us servicemembers and chinese civilians.&nbsp;

grant to dr. john lardas modern
agency: national endowment for the humanities
archival research in support of a book on the social, economic, and technological history of akron, ohio.&nbsp;

grant to dr. tanya e. erzen
agency: national endowment for the humanities
research and writing of a book on gender, girlhood, and incarceration in washington state between 1915 and the 1990s.&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;

grant to dr. charlotte conover gordon
agency: national endowment for the humanities
research and writing of a group biography of lucretia mott (1793-1880), sojourner truth (1797-1883), lucy stone (1818-1893), and frances ellen watkins harper (1825-1911), four women reformers who used the lecture circuit to fight for abolition and women’s rights.&nbsp;

grant to university of southern california
agency: national endowment for the humanities
a&nbsp;foundations project to plan for the accessibility of&nbsp;a dataset&nbsp;documenting&nbsp;demographics and social change in the city of los angeles and 86 los angeles county municipalities between 1950 and 2010.&nbsp;
